{"id": "4664", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=4664", "title": "Brewster (Massachusetts)", "text": "Brewster is in Massachusetts on Cape Cod. Brewster, known as a favorite home of sea captains, is a charming bayside town. It quieter than many Cape towns and is home to Nickerson State park, a preserve of 400 acres of trails.\nGet around.\nCar or bicycle are preferred.\nBuy.\nBrewster has numerous galleries and shops to browse.\nSleep.\nHundreds of campsites available at Nickerson State Park and Sweetwater Forest, see Parks section for more details.\nGo next.\nOrleans is just a bicycle ride away. Provincetown and Chatham are favorite shopping trips for those days that are just wrong for the beach."}
{"id": "4665", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=4665", "title": "Brewster (New York)", "text": "Brewster is a town in Putnam County in New York.\nGet in.\nBy plane.\nThe nearest airports are Westchester County Airport in White Plains/Harrison, NY and New York Stewart International Airport in Newburgh, NY\nBy train.\nMetro North commuter train arrive from Grand Central and 125th St. in New York (city) and other places south.\nBy car.\nI-684 North to exit 10 then turn right onto Rt 22 which leads to downtown Brewster Village. I-84 East to I-684 north is used when coming from CT.\nBuy.\nThere are a handful of department stores in town including Marshall's and Kohl's, and the Danbury Fair Mall is fifteen minutes away in Danbury."}
{"id": "4666", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=4666", "title": "Brewster (Ohio)", "text": "Brewster is a village in Stark County, Ohio.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nBrewster lies on the junction of US 62 and SR 93."}
