{"id": "4703", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=4703", "title": "Bridgnorth", "text": "Bridgnorth is a historic market market town on the banks of the River Severn in Shropshire, England. The town is built on two levels, with the upper level dominated by the remains of a medieval castle keep which leans at an angle greater than the leaning tower of Pisa.\nGet in.\nBy train.\nBridgnorth station is no longer part of National Rail and instead used for the Severn Valley Railway.\nThe nearest stations are in Telford (about 12.5 mi away), Shrewsbury (about 15 mi away) and Wolverhampton (about 18.7 mi away) respectively.\nGo next.\nMap of places with Wikivoyage articles nearby"}
